# wowzaV9-Pro
# ============
# This repo is a REBUILD, not a fork.
#
# The folder it lives in was previously v10 (v9's staging sandbox) and still holds a stale
# copy of v9 at commit 12a3dc8 on disk. Prompt 2 section 3 says never delete those research
# assets, so they stay exactly where they are — but they are NOT committed here. Code is
# ported into src/ deliberately, module by module, each with an OLD / NEW / WHY / RISK note.
# Inheriting a stale clone wholesale would reintroduce bugs v9 has since fixed.
#
# Strategy: ignore every root entry, then re-admit only the Pro tree.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/.github/
!/README.md
!/docs/
!/config/
!/src/
!/registry/
!/experiments/
!/tests/
!/data/
!/models/
!/output/

# ── Secrets: never, by any path ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# v10's .env carries live API-Football, Google and GitHub credentials. They must reach CI as
# repository secrets, never as a committed file.
.env
.env.*
.api_keys
**/secrets.toml
**/bot_config.json
*.pem
*.key

# ── Large or regenerable data ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Pro season store is built by importers from v9's committed output (the pattern v11
# already uses: read the baseline's public data over HTTP). Committing 187MB of legacy
# parquet and backtest CSVs would tax every clone forever for data we can rebuild.
*.parquet
*.xlsx
*.zip
data/**
models/**
output/**

# ...but keep the empty scaffolding and the small machine-readable truth files.
!data/.gitkeep
!models/.gitkeep
!output/.gitkeep
!output/system_registry.json
!output/pro_readiness.json
!registry/**
!experiments/**/manifest.json
!experiments/**/metrics.json
!experiments/**/by_league.csv
!experiments/**/calibration.csv

# ── Caches ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
**/*_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
